# Store every file exactly as it is on disk: no text / EOL normalisation anywhere.
#
# Why: core.autocrlf=true was silently LF-normalising text blobs, so the repository copy of
# a file could be "same content, different bytes" from the byte-frozen deposit member
# (e.g. derived_data/figure_source_data/fig2a_tmb_dist.tsv: 1,299,133 B on disk vs a
# 1,269,355 B blob).  The public snapshot is advertised as byte-reproducible against the
# deposit, so the repository must store the same bytes.
#
# `* -text` disables conversion for every path (including future ones).
* -text

# ...but keep text diffing/merging for the file types we actually read and review.
*.R     diff
*.py    diff
*.md    diff
*.tsv   diff
*.csv   diff
*.txt   diff
*.json  diff
*.sh    diff
*.lock  diff
